        "original_id": "c908662b-7363-52b2-a2f4-c6eb93095f34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mel Brooks, Alan Johnson, Charles Durning\n- Films: To Be or Not to Be, Silent Movie, The Sting, Dog Day Afternoon, The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas, Tootsie\n- Companies: 20th Century Fox\n- Topics: American war comedy films, satirical comedy films\n\nFacts:\n- Mel Brooks was born as Melvin Kaminsky on June 28, 1926.\n- Silent Movie is a 1976 American satirical comedy film that Mel Brooks co-wrote, directed, and starred in.\n- 20th Century Fox released Silent Movie on June 17, 1976.\n- Charles Durning's best-known film roles included The Sting (1973) and Dog Day Afternoon (1975).\n- Charles Durning's best-known comedy film roles included The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas (1982), Tootsie (1982), and To Be or Not to Be (1983).\n- To Be or Not to Be is a 1983 American war comedy film directed by Alan Johnson and produced by Mel Brooks.\n- Mel Brooks is an American actor, writer, producer, director, comedian, and composer.",
